# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Map-of-record candidates + large regenerable OpenDRIVE artifacts (up to
# ~130 MB). These are content-addressed via sha256 in acceptance JSONs and
# the C1 pin packages (c1_pin_package.json) and regenerable by
# scripts/regen_map_of_record.py; the binaries themselves never enter git.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
campaigns/*/candidate/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WS5 (map-quality/RQ hardening plan, 2026-09-02): formalizing large-artifact
# exclusions that had accumulated as untracked clutter for weeks. All are
# regenerable (pipeline regen / GNN retrain) or intermediate working state,
# not source-of-truth. Small summary/stats JSONs alongside them remain
# tracked where present (matching the C2/C2-R2 pattern above).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Full per-run regen working directories (seed XODR, pipeline_out/, logs --
# tens of GB across a session; the emitted candidate is separately excluded
# above, and small evidence reports referencing a run are committed
# individually, not the whole run directory).
campaigns/*/regen/
# GNN training checkpoints (large .pt files; the seed run reports/aggregate
# stats JSONs alongside them remain tracked).
reports/post_audit_hardening/*/checkpoints/
reports/post_audit_hardening/*/*/checkpoints/
# GNN tile corpora used for training/eval (large XODR tile sets; not the
# small per-tile metrics/reports).
reports/post_audit_hardening/*/union_tiles/
reports/post_audit_hardening/*/manual_tiles/
reports/post_audit_hardening/_e2_proto.xodr
reports/post_audit_hardening/_e2_proto_linkoffset.xodr
reports/post_audit_hardening/_e2_proto_locked.xodr
reports/post_audit_hardening/_gen_watch_log/
reports/post_audit_hardening/_proc_smoke_log/
reports/post_audit_hardening/_manual_reverify_*/
